       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I know I said earlier that I would if the dose was intentional. On reflection, I shouldn't, because 1000 mg/day is 5 times the maximum labeled dose. I'm not aware of any indication or protocol that supports it, and it could seriously harm the patient. I'd rather say that now than put the order in the queue.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a different dose.** Tell me the dose, such as 100 mg or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Enter it with a documented rationale.** If a specific clinical reason or protocol supports this dose, send it to me. I'll reconsider and put it in the order note.\n- **Use another route.** If you need to override the dose limit, you can go through pharmacy or a direct order-entry override. Those routes have pharmacist verification and clinical decision support.\n\nIf the concern is a possible overdose or ingestion, please contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology. Treatment there is supportive and doesn't involve ordering the drug."
      }
